From febfcae868ac26c2534ab7709a5e8183fb4fc3dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: martinsngr <martin.sinegre@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:22:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] F: velocity of cells with Darcy and non-Darcy faces
 consistent with the fluxes

Change B made porous faces with small Darcy number "Darcy faces": their
total flux is phiDarcyExplicit - Mf*snGrad(p), with the Darcy mobility Mf.
Cells with only Darcy faces take U = reconstruct(phi); the others keep the
momentum velocity U = HbyA + rAU*reconstruct(((phiG + phiPc) -
pEqn.flux())/rAUf). On their Darcy faces pEqn.flux() is built with Mf, so
dividing it by rAUf made the pressure part Mf/rAUf times too large (about
10 for air, 200 for water at dt 1e-7). The cell velocity drifted from the
face fluxes by metres per second per step (2D bench: 39 m/s after 10 steps
in porous cells next to free cells, while their face fluxes gave 0.05-0.9
m/s; single-yarn case: 2.3e4 m/s in wall cells). Through HbyA and ddtCorr
this velocity enters the flux of the cell's non-Darcy faces.

1. pEqn.H: the face driving force of the U correction uses the mobility of
   each face's own flux: (phiG + phiPc)/rAUf on momentum faces,
   phiDarcyExplicit/Mf on Darcy faces, and snGrad(p)*|Sf| for the pressure
   part on all faces. Identical to the previous expression on momentum
   faces.
2. createPorousMediaFields.H: non-coupled boundary faces with a fixed
   velocity (walls, fixed inflow) no longer prevent a cell from being a
   Darcy cell: their flux uses the boundary value of U, never the cell
   value, and ddtCorr is zero there.

Checks: no change where all porous cells are Darcy cells (all-porous 2D
bench to 0.2 ms bit-identical); single-yarn case (Darcy cells except
along its closed wall): alpha, p and phi bit-identical over 225 steps, only
the written U changes there (max 2.3e4 -> 18.9 m/s, p99 4 m/s).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hybridPorousInterFoam/createPorousMediaFields.H | 10 +++++++++-
 hybridPorousInterFoam/pEqn.H                    | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hybridPorousInterFoam/createPorousMediaFields.H b/hybridPorousInterFoam/createPorousMediaFields.H
index fe2f237..cf5c79e 100644
--- a/hybridPorousInterFoam/createPorousMediaFields.H
+++ b/hybridPorousInterFoam/createPorousMediaFields.H
@@ -161,7 +161,10 @@ surfaceScalarField DarcyFace("DarcyFace", 0*Solidf);
 
 // Cells whose faces are all Darcy faces: their velocity is the one of the
 // Darcy flux. Other porous cells keep the momentum-equation velocity, which
-// the non-Darcy faces around them use.
+// the non-Darcy faces around them use. Non-coupled boundary faces with a
+// fixed velocity (walls, fixed inflow) are not counted: their flux uses the
+// boundary value of U, never the cell value (and ddtCorr is zero there), so
+// they do not need the momentum velocity of the cell (change F).
 volScalarField DarcyCell("DarcyCell", Solid);
 {
     const labelUList& own = mesh.owner();
@@ -176,6 +179,11 @@ volScalarField DarcyCell("DarcyCell", Solid);
     }
     forAll(DarcyFace.boundaryField(), patchi)
     {
+        const fvPatchVectorField& Up = U.boundaryField()[patchi];
+        if (!Up.coupled() && Up.fixesValue())
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
         const labelUList& fc = mesh.boundary()[patchi].faceCells();
         forAll(fc, facei)
         {
diff --git a/hybridPorousInterFoam/pEqn.H b/hybridPorousInterFoam/pEqn.H
index f437a72..fbe6f11 100644
--- a/hybridPorousInterFoam/pEqn.H
+++ b/hybridPorousInterFoam/pEqn.H
@@ -84,7 +84,20 @@
 
             p.relax();
 
-            U = HbyA + rAU()*fvc::reconstruct(((phiG+phiPc) - pEqn.flux())/rAUf);
+            // Change F: the face driving force of the U correction must use
+            // the mobility of the face's own flux: momentum faces
+            // (phiG + phiPc)/rAUf, Darcy faces phiDarcyExplicit/Mf, and the
+            // pressure gradient snGrad(p) on all (pEqn.flux()/rAUf was
+            // Mf/rAUf times too large on Darcy faces). Same as before on
+            // momentum faces; cells with only Darcy faces are overwritten
+            // below.
+            U = HbyA + rAU()*fvc::reconstruct
+            (
+                (1. - DarcyFace)*(phiG + phiPc)/rAUf
+              + DarcyFace*phiDarcyExplicit
+               /max(Mf, dimensionedScalar(Mf.dimensions(), vSmall))
+              - fvc::snGrad(p)*mesh.magSf()
+            );
             // cells with only Darcy faces: velocity of the Darcy flux
             U = (1. - DarcyCell)*U + DarcyCell*fvc::reconstruct(phi);
             U.correctBoundaryConditions();
